# borrowed-view parallel-tree-learning A/B bench
# commit:       fe2d3a27 (perf(tree_learn): borrowed-view parallel path)
# vs baseline:  90b68279 (docs(CLAUDE): strict 1.20x cjxl target hit)
# hardware:     AMD Ryzen 9 7950X (16C/32T water-cooled)
# build:        cargo build --release -p jxl-encoder --features 'profile-phases parallel parallel-tree-learning'
#               NO -C target-cpu=native (per CLAUDE.md benchmark rules)
# threads:      8 (CLIFF_THREADS=8 from lossless_cliff_profile harness)
# effort:       7 (lossless)
# date:         2026-05-16T17:25Z
# system load:  ~5 during bench (concurrent agent encoding workload)
#
# Method: paired interleaved A/B per iter; random order each iter to amortize
# thermal/load bias. Each iter runs ONE encode through lossless_cliff_profile
# (CLIFF_SAMPLES=1), captures best_ms (=only_ms) and the
# modular/compute_best_tree phase.
